Looking at the code and intent now. Let me verify each candidate against the actual source.
All candidates verified against source. Confirmed: `compact_tombstones` is never called from any normal-operation path (only `clear` touches tombstones directly at line 146); `get_by_handle` never reads `handle.generation` or `entry.generation` despite both fields existing; `evict_one` pops back (MRU) not front (LRU).

I'm declining the `cache.rs:70` candidate (replace-skips-eviction). A1's invariant "number of live entries never exceeds capacity" holds on replace since count doesn't increase; the literal "evicts exactly one entry first" describes the mechanism for new entries, and evicting on replace would be over-eviction. Not a real defect.

